{"task_id": "Mbpp/99", "solution": "def decimal_to_binary(decimal: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a non-negative integer to its binary string representation.\n    Includes input validation for type and non-negativity.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(decimal, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be of type int.\")\n    if decimal < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a non\u2011negative integer.\")\n\n    if decimal == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n\n    bits = []\n    n = decimal\n    while n > 0:\n        bits.append(str(n & 1))\n        n >>= 1\n    return \"\".join(reversed(bits))"}
